<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Excludes files that are pure OS/hardware or process interop (Win32 capture, WGC frame pump,
  file/JSON I/O, the named-pipe channel, each exe's entry point) from the coverage gate. These
  have no branching business logic worth pinning with unit tests and can't run without a live
  display or a second process; they're verified manually and via the replay/parity regression
  tests instead. Excluding a file only affects the aggregate percentage, never whether anything
  in it gets tested.

  Everything else stays gated — the contracts, the plugins' parser/state-machine/ledger code, the
  engine's scan loop, subscription registry, gRPC service, OCR pipeline and hotkey parsing, and
  the SDK's tick mapping.

  Carried over from the monolith's tests/TrackingService.Tests/coverlet.runsettings and re-pointed
  at the engine/plugin layout after ENGINE-SPLIT TASK-8 retired src/TrackingService. The list is
  the old one with three deliberate adjustments, each noted because the layout forced a choice:

  - Trackers/TrackerHost.cs and Trackers/FrameDumpTracker.cs are gone with the files. ScanLoop,
    which replaced TrackerHost, is directly tested and therefore stays gated.
  - Core/ProbeConfig.cs became Core/EngineConfig.cs, still excluded — it is the same
    exists/write-defaults/deserialize body. The plugins' MissionConfig.cs and RefineryConfig.cs
    are NOT excluded despite the same shape: RefineryConfig.ResolveLedgerPath carries the rule
    that keeps a replay from writing into real order history, and LedgerTargetTests pins it.
  - Core/LiveFrameSource.cs is added: it is the WGC frame pump extracted out of the monolith's
    MonitorCapture path, and like MonitorCapture it cannot run without a live capture session.

  TASK-8's brief also listed Core/HotkeyListener.cs and Core/OcrPipeline.cs as process-edge files
  to exclude. They are deliberately NOT excluded, because the same task moved 28 tests onto their
  pure helpers (ParseHotkey, EffectiveScale, CropAndScale, the language diagnostics). Excluding
  them would hide the most-tested arithmetic in the engine from the gate, which contradicts the
  instruction to keep the previously-gated bar unchanged — the monolith gated both files too.
  They read low (mixed pure helpers plus OS-bound async methods); that is expected, not a gap.

  As before, there is no numeric threshold here: the gate is this exclusion policy, and the bar is
  read off the aggregate.

  Usage (from the repo root):
    dotnet test StarCitizenTracker.slnx --settings coverlet.runsettings --collect:"XPlat Code Coverage"
-->
<RunSettings>
  <DataCollectionRunSettings>
    <DataCollectors>
      <DataCollector friendlyName="XPlat code coverage">
        <Configuration>
          <Format>cobertura</Format>
          <ExcludeByFile>
            **/Core/CaptureInterop.cs,
            **/Core/MonitorCapture.cs,
            **/Core/LiveFrameSource.cs,
            **/Core/FrameSaver.cs,
            **/Core/EngineConfig.cs,
            **/ConsoleSink.cs,
            **/NamedPipeChannel.cs,
            **/Metrics/MetricsSampler.cs,
            **/Metrics/MetricsReporter.cs,
            **/Program.cs
          </ExcludeByFile>
        </Configuration>
      </DataCollector>
    </DataCollectors>
  </DataCollectionRunSettings>
</RunSettings>
